WEBVTT

00:03:58.336 --> 00:04:02.036
where they spend the first decade
or two of their adult life

00:04:02.060 --> 00:04:03.977
somehow climbing Mountain One,

00:04:04.001 --> 00:04:07.545
and then they have this midlife crisis
or moment of realization,

00:04:07.569 --> 00:04:10.407
and they enter more a life of meaning
or pursuit of meaning?

00:04:10.431 --> 00:04:13.452
DB: I think most people live
what the culture wants them to live

00:04:13.476 --> 00:04:14.627
for some time.

00:04:14.651 --> 00:04:15.858
It can happen at any age.

00:04:15.882 --> 00:04:17.327
Then they make this discovery.

00:04:17.351 --> 00:04:20.861
So they get out of college, say, and
have a career they're going to build.

00:04:20.885 --> 00:04:22.697
"I'm going to be a doctor or lawyer."

00:04:22.721 --> 00:04:25.703
And then, they either achieve
success and find it unsatisfying,

00:04:25.727 --> 00:04:27.807
or they fail, they're not
on their mountain.

00:04:27.831 --> 00:04:30.747
Or something bad happens
that's not part of the original plan: